PLACEHOLDER — no trusted release-signing public key has been added yet.

This file must contain the ASCII-armored GPG public key(s) that
.github/workflows/release.yml trusts when verifying a release tag's
signature. It is not a secret: it only ever holds public key material,
and changes to it go through normal pull request review, which is what
makes a future key swap or compromise visible.

To populate it with the key matching the current
OPENBAO_SECRET_SYNC_RELEASE_TAG_GPG_PRIVATE_KEY secret, run the
"Release Tag" workflow once and copy the exported public key block from
its job summary (see the "Export release tag signing public key" step
in .github/workflows/release-tag.yml), or run locally:

    gpg --export --armor "<RELEASE_TAG_SIGNING_FINGERPRINT>" > .github/release-signing-keys.asc

Then replace this placeholder text with the real
"-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----" ... "-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----"
content and submit it as its own reviewed pull request.

Until this file contains a real public key, the "Verify release tag"
step in .github/workflows/release.yml will fail closed rather than
silently accept an unverified tag.
